{
  "about": "Every Toybox component, the file that holds it (under packages/shell/src/ui/), the design-system section, its accessibility role, how it takes its testID and the parts it derives. inPairCell = screens put the component in a usePairLayout cell, so its layoutStyle must grow, never flex: 1 (the pair-cell-flex rule); owner = the skill that ships the template; check-components.mjs checks the files this skill owns and only the existence of the others.",
  "prerequisites": [
    {
      "file": "packages/shell/src/theme/tokens.ts",
      "owner": "toybox-design-system"
    },
    {
      "file": "packages/shell/src/theme/shell-colors.ts",
      "owner": "toybox-design-system"
    },
    {
      "file": "packages/shell/src/theme/motion.ts",
      "owner": "toybox-design-system"
    },
    {
      "file": "packages/shell/src/theme/make-styles.ts",
      "owner": "toybox-design-system"
    },
    {
      "file": "packages/shell/src/theme/type-styles.ts",
      "owner": "toybox-design-system",
      "mustContain": "rowLabelStrong",
      "why": "ListRow's strong and danger labels use TYPE_STYLES.rowLabelStrong (17 Bold, 1.32 / 1.5)"
    },
    {
      "file": "packages/shell/src/ui/app-text.tsx",
      "owner": "toybox-design-system"
    },
    {
      "file": "packages/shell/src/ui/raised-surface.tsx",
      "owner": "toybox-design-system",
      "mustContain": "top: elevation",
      "why": "a pushed-in key (the chosen segment, a locked level tile) must sit elevation lower by layout, where Maestro and the parity bounds measure it, not by a transform"
    },
    {
      "file": "packages/shell/src/ui/toybox-styles.ts",
      "owner": "toybox-design-system"
    },
    {
